// ============================================================================
// fc.diag.v1 — the engine's diagnostic probes, triggered by an operator.
//
// One service, one RPC: DiagService.RunProbe. The only client is the scraper's
// own CLI (dist/diag/run.js), run as a Kubernetes Job that Ross triggers or
// arms; it reaches the engine over gRPC (h2c inside Linkerd mTLS). Connect over
// HTTP/1.1 is not a supported transport for this service.
//
// WHY IT EXISTS. Some stores bar AI agents by name. Claude and its tools never
// contact those hosts. When passive evidence (logs, /health/detailed, the
// fetch_failure ledger) is not enough, a probe sends at most a handful of
// requests through the engine's own lanes, and the result is read afterwards.
// Every request a probe may send is bounded twice by the engine: per call
// (the probe's hard maximum) and per host (a rolling 24 h cap).
//
// FIDELITY: instants are RFC 3339 UTC strings; sha256 values are lowercase hex
// (the same spelling as the robots pins they are compared with); nothing here
// is a float or a Struct. The canary item id is never carried in either
// direction: the engine resolves it and labels its target role CANARY.
// ============================================================================

